LeetCode 46 – Permutations
Problem Description

Given an array of distinct integers nums, return all the possible permutations. You can return the answer in any order.

A permutation is an arrangement of all elements in a specific order.

Approach: Iterative Permutation Building

This solution uses an iterative insertion approach to generate all possible permutations.

Instead of using recursion or backtracking, we build permutations step by step by inserting each new number into every possible position of the existing permutations.

Algorithm
Initialize perms with an empty permutation: [[]].
Iterate through each number in nums.
Create a new list new_perms to store updated permutations.
For every existing permutation:
Try inserting the current number at every possible index.
Create a copy of the permutation.
Insert the number at the chosen position.
Add the resulting permutation to new_perms.
Update perms with new_perms.
Return all generated permutations.


Example

Input:

python
nums = [1, 2, 3]


Output:

python
[
    [3, 2, 1],
    [2, 3, 1],
    [2, 1, 3],
    [3, 1, 2],
    [1, 3, 2],
    [1, 2, 3]
]

Complexity Analysis

Let n be the number of elements in the input array.

Time Complexity: O(n × n!) – There are n! permutations, and generating each permutation involves copying and inserting elements, which takes up to O(n) time.
Space Complexity: O(n × n!) – We store all n! permutations, each containing n elements.
Key Takeaway

This approach generates permutations iteratively by inserting each new element into every possible position of previously generated permutations.

It is an alternative to the commonly used backtracking approach and avoids recursive function calls.
